{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head c5d3c008a53ed1639cfeff6367824470c517670e on builder/rr1-do-rate-20261117, all 5 artifacts, for request 5b925de2 under my promise 2ab323d7. The implementation is RR-1 (request d4cc718e, promise 14c8fb45), with the `--all` option asked for in decision 9f19644e. The reporting artifact is the RR-1 note.\n\nThe head's parent is fc42cf3e. Main has since moved to a7acfdf2 (AR-4, AR-5 and HL-1), and none of the head's 5 paths overlaps those landings. `git merge-tree --write-tree a7acfdf2 c5d3c008` merges cleanly to tree 1869e887.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The note first, then the whole diff.\n- `scripts/do-rate.mjs`. It queries `durableObjectsInvocationsAdaptiveGroups` at the one fixed endpoint `https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/graphql`, grouped by minute and Worker. `readRows` asks for at most 10,000 groups. A reply at that limit splits the window in half and reads each half, and a one-minute window at the limit fails, so the script never reports a truncated reply. `aggregate` fills every minute with zeros and fails on a minute outside the window or a Worker outside the query. The defaults come from `deploy-config.mjs`. `--all` names no Worker in the query and lists every Worker with rows. It and `--worker` exclude each other. The script imports only Node built-ins and `deploy-config.mjs`.\n- `scripts/do-rate.test.mjs` runs on a recorded reply with no network, and `scripts/test.mjs` adds it to the Node stage.\n- `docs/operate-a-service.md` adds step 7, the rate read after the smoke checks, and moves the old step 7 to step 8.\n\nRequest conditions (d4cc718e):\n\n1. Window by `--since`/`--until` or `--minutes`, and the token from `--token-file` or `CLOUDFLARE_ANALYTICS_TOKEN`: met.\n2. Per-minute lines, totals, the per-hour rate and `--baseline` flags: met.\n3. A unit case on a recorded response: met, 10 tests.\n4. The docs entry beside `deploy.mjs`: met, step 7.\n5. No new package: met. `package.json` and the lockfile do not change.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- The unit test. `node --test scripts/do-rate.test.mjs` passes 10 of 10 in 0.1 s. This is the one light probe I ran.\n- The live read. `artroom-evidence/2026-11-17-rr1-witness/do-rate-15min.txt` reads 14:29Z to 14:44Z: dap-grow 49 a minute, 3,340.0 an hour; dap-lending 14 in the window; exit 0. The file contains no token text. The witness ran on the first head 4ba00ab5, before `--all`, so the `--all` path has unit cases only.\n- The gate. Run 2 (END e8ef993a) passed at this head: plain 4,998 and native 1,192. The last lines of `gate.txt` read \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\".\n- Scope. The 5 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only fc42cf3e c5d3c008`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean.\n- Wake rate. The script is an operator tool that runs once per call. It adds no alarm, retry or scheduled pass to any Worker.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The rate read that every deployment now owes moves from the planner's scratchpad into a reviewed script with a documented step. Splitting at the row limit is better than trusting a reply that may be cut short.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. The token goes only into the `authorization` header to the fixed Cloudflare endpoint. `say()` replaces any token text in output and errors, the token file must hold one token-shaped line or `KEY=value` lines, and the unexpected-failure path prints no message text. The repository holds no account ID or token. The token needs only Account Analytics read.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nFact for the planner: no deployment follows this head. The next deployment can use step 7 in place of the scratch script, and the first `--all` run in use is its live check.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push or landing. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git